<section class="page-hero">
      <div class="wrap"><div class="page-hero__eyebrow">Legal</div><h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__sub">We're committed to digital and physical access for everyone.</p></div>
    </section>
    <article class="legal-body">
      <h2>Our commitment</h2>
      <p>Once Upon A Time, Inc. strives to meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA for all digital content. We design, develop, and test with accessibility in mind, and treat every accessibility report as a priority bug.</p>
      <h2>Digital features</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keyboard navigation across every interactive element</li>
        <li>Visible focus indicators that meet 3:1 contrast minimum</li>
        <li>Semantic HTML and ARIA used to label form fields, regions, and live updates</li>
        <li>Color contrast for body text meets 4.5:1; large text meets 3:1</li>
        <li>Reduced-motion preference respected for animations and scrolling</li>
        <li>Alt text on every meaningful image</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Physical access</h2>
      <p>Our studio at 87-61 111th St, Richmond Hill, NY 11418 has step-free entry from the street, an accessible restroom, and wheelchair-accessible studios on the ground floor. If you have specific access needs for a class, please email us in advance.</p>
      <h2>Reporting an issue</h2>
      <p>Found something that doesn't meet the bar? Please email <a href="mailto:contact@onceuponatime.org?subject=Accessibility%20feedback">contact@onceuponatime.org</a> with the page URL and a description. We aim to respond within 2 business days.</p>
      <h2>Ongoing work</h2>
      <p>We test with screen readers (VoiceOver, NVDA), audit color contrast each release, and conduct an external accessibility review annually. Most recent review: April 2026.</p>
    </article>

